`catalog show|check` (#980 C1c): the deployment catalog, a file the
deployment provisions to its owners and to the far side of a constrained face
(core §8.6). It is never fetched and never served, so neither verb opens a
session. `zk2 catalog new|add` writes one; these read it.

`show` reads one catalog: its id first, alone on its line, its epoch, and
every entry, each with whether `--contracts` holds that revision.

```console
$ zenctl catalog show --catalog ../examples/zk2/zenoh-modem/catalog.json --contracts ../examples/zk2/zenoh-modem/modem.v3.toml --format table
36c25c0f
file      ../examples/zk2/zenoh-modem/catalog.json
epoch     1767225600 (2026-01-01T00:00:00Z)
succeeds  0a90fd61 (3 entries)
succeeds  ea268fad (5 entries)
  0  modem.v3   sha256:9a3e2859a538a95daafc53e7dffe8c9d0610312f7650f27250b9e6fee0965953  not held
  1  config.v1  sha256:727ff0090b99ad8fc09b5398804d1a14288bebf661f374ec6904351344a1a7b1  not held
  2  health.v1  sha256:e9dbcdcb2fc325ca3121fdcacf7badd0091f62d97ab4c7d7a5f022dd8d6671df  not held
  3  config.v1  sha256:4778b0aae3ce092a5a61386c8616cd4470534e354b35bdc9666c75c601ad4501  not held
  4  health.v1  sha256:60a4374513172609a9140051bb9b5bd9abc898ed6c22035c303414795940e42f  not held
  5  modem.v3   sha256:69081ed3aae72b1e6a869a260c234ba5f2bf0b8c63069f55e396a96b677e7d66  held

```

```console
$ zenctl catalog show --catalog ../examples/zk2/zenoh-modem/catalog.json --format ndjson
{"epoch":1767225600,"epoch_utc":"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z","id":"36c25c0f","lineage":[{"entries":3,"id":"0a90fd61"},{"entries":5,"id":"ea268fad"}],"path":"../examples/zk2/zenoh-modem/catalog.json","report":"catalog"}
{"contract":"sha256:9a3e2859a538a95daafc53e7dffe8c9d0610312f7650f27250b9e6fee0965953","iface":"modem.v3","index":0,"row":"entry"}
{"contract":"sha256:727ff0090b99ad8fc09b5398804d1a14288bebf661f374ec6904351344a1a7b1","iface":"config.v1","index":1,"row":"entry"}
{"contract":"sha256:e9dbcdcb2fc325ca3121fdcacf7badd0091f62d97ab4c7d7a5f022dd8d6671df","iface":"health.v1","index":2,"row":"entry"}
{"contract":"sha256:4778b0aae3ce092a5a61386c8616cd4470534e354b35bdc9666c75c601ad4501","iface":"config.v1","index":3,"row":"entry"}
{"contract":"sha256:60a4374513172609a9140051bb9b5bd9abc898ed6c22035c303414795940e42f","iface":"health.v1","index":4,"row":"entry"}
{"contract":"sha256:69081ed3aae72b1e6a869a260c234ba5f2bf0b8c63069f55e396a96b677e7d66","iface":"modem.v3","index":5,"row":"entry"}

```

`check` is a judgement on the one contract in `zenctl/src/exit.rs`. The ground
side holds the same catalog and checks it against its own contracts: each one
in it, exit 0.

```console
$ zenctl catalog check --catalog ../examples/zk2/zenoh-modem/catalog.json --contracts ../examples/zk2/zenoh-modem/modem.v3.toml --format table
36c25c0f
file      ../examples/zk2/zenoh-modem/catalog.json
epoch     1767225600 (2026-01-01T00:00:00Z)
succeeds  0a90fd61 (3 entries)
succeeds  ea268fad (5 entries)
  0  modem.v3   sha256:9a3e2859a538a95daafc53e7dffe8c9d0610312f7650f27250b9e6fee0965953  not held
  1  config.v1  sha256:727ff0090b99ad8fc09b5398804d1a14288bebf661f374ec6904351344a1a7b1  not held
  2  health.v1  sha256:e9dbcdcb2fc325ca3121fdcacf7badd0091f62d97ab4c7d7a5f022dd8d6671df  not held
  3  config.v1  sha256:4778b0aae3ce092a5a61386c8616cd4470534e354b35bdc9666c75c601ad4501  not held
  4  health.v1  sha256:60a4374513172609a9140051bb9b5bd9abc898ed6c22035c303414795940e42f  not held
  5  modem.v3   sha256:69081ed3aae72b1e6a869a260c234ba5f2bf0b8c63069f55e396a96b677e7d66  held

```

A revision in hand that the catalog lacks has no index a far side can read:
the finding, exit 1.

```console
$ zenctl catalog check --catalog ../examples/zk2/zenoh-modem/catalog.json --contracts ../examples/zk2/walkthrough/camera.v1.toml --format table
? 1
36c25c0f
file      ../examples/zk2/zenoh-modem/catalog.json
epoch     1767225600 (2026-01-01T00:00:00Z)
succeeds  0a90fd61 (3 entries)
succeeds  ea268fad (5 entries)
  0  modem.v3   sha256:9a3e2859a538a95daafc53e7dffe8c9d0610312f7650f27250b9e6fee0965953  not held
  1  config.v1  sha256:727ff0090b99ad8fc09b5398804d1a14288bebf661f374ec6904351344a1a7b1  not held
  2  health.v1  sha256:e9dbcdcb2fc325ca3121fdcacf7badd0091f62d97ab4c7d7a5f022dd8d6671df  not held
  3  config.v1  sha256:4778b0aae3ce092a5a61386c8616cd4470534e354b35bdc9666c75c601ad4501  not held
  4  health.v1  sha256:60a4374513172609a9140051bb9b5bd9abc898ed6c22035c303414795940e42f  not held
  5  modem.v3   sha256:69081ed3aae72b1e6a869a260c234ba5f2bf0b8c63069f55e396a96b677e7d66  not held
  missing  camera.v1  sha256:0f66b421dc6decf2b28bf4b8f0c6006cbdbb7fe0a4d9a997e637f9105dc0ea98
a revision the catalog lacks has no index a far side can read: append it with `zk2 catalog add` and provision the successor (core §8.6)

```

Its successor appends `camera.v1` at index 3, and keeps the epoch and every
earlier index: it succeeds the catalog it extends. That catalog is
zenoh-modem's before #978's F4 appended `config.v1` and `health.v1`'s
revisions 1.1, kept as a fixture.

```console
$ zenctl catalog check --catalog tests/cmd/fixtures/catalog/successor.json --previous tests/cmd/fixtures/catalog/zenoh-modem-0a90fd61.json --contracts ../examples/zk2/walkthrough/camera.v1.toml --format table
9da7c4a4
file      tests/cmd/fixtures/catalog/successor.json
epoch     1767225600 (2026-01-01T00:00:00Z)
succeeds  0a90fd61 (3 entries)
previous  0a90fd61 (succeeds)
  0  modem.v3   sha256:9a3e2859a538a95daafc53e7dffe8c9d0610312f7650f27250b9e6fee0965953  not held
  1  config.v1  sha256:727ff0090b99ad8fc09b5398804d1a14288bebf661f374ec6904351344a1a7b1  not held
  2  health.v1  sha256:e9dbcdcb2fc325ca3121fdcacf7badd0091f62d97ab4c7d7a5f022dd8d6671df  not held
  3  camera.v1  sha256:0f66b421dc6decf2b28bf4b8f0c6006cbdbb7fe0a4d9a997e637f9105dc0ea98  held

```

One that moves the epoch does not, and the first refusal that applies is named
by its token.

```console
$ zenctl catalog check --catalog tests/cmd/fixtures/catalog/moved.json --previous tests/cmd/fixtures/catalog/zenoh-modem-0a90fd61.json --format table
? 1
ce400794
file      tests/cmd/fixtures/catalog/moved.json
epoch     0 (1970-01-01T00:00:00Z)
succeeds  0a90fd61 (3 entries)
previous  0a90fd61: the epoch moved (epoch_moved)
  0  modem.v3   sha256:9a3e2859a538a95daafc53e7dffe8c9d0610312f7650f27250b9e6fee0965953
  1  config.v1  sha256:727ff0090b99ad8fc09b5398804d1a14288bebf661f374ec6904351344a1a7b1
  2  health.v1  sha256:e9dbcdcb2fc325ca3121fdcacf7badd0091f62d97ab4c7d7a5f022dd8d6671df
  3  camera.v1  sha256:0f66b421dc6decf2b28bf4b8f0c6006cbdbb7fe0a4d9a997e637f9105dc0ea98

```

A document §8.6's reading refuses is the finding too, its refusal's token
named. Elsewhere a refused `--catalog` is refused input, exit 2.

```console
$ zenctl catalog check --catalog tests/cmd/fixtures/catalog/refused.json --format table
? 1
tests/cmd/fixtures/catalog/refused.json: refused — catalog: epoch or entries missing, or a member besides format, epoch, entries and lineage (member)

```

```console
$ zenctl catalog show --catalog tests/cmd/fixtures/catalog/refused.json --format table
? 2
Error: --catalog tests/cmd/fixtures/catalog/refused.json: refused — catalog: epoch or entries missing, or a member besides format, epoch, entries and lineage (member)

```

```console
$ zenctl catalog show --format table
? 2
Error: --catalog is required: the catalog file to read

```

`schema show` prints a revision's index in each catalog given, and says where
one does not list it.

```console
$ zenctl schema show camera.v1 --contracts ../examples/zk2/walkthrough/camera.v1.toml --catalog ../examples/zk2/zenoh-modem/catalog.json --catalog tests/cmd/fixtures/catalog/successor.json --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5 --format table
camera.v1 sha256:0f66b421dc6decf2b28bf4b8f0c6006cbdbb7fe0a4d9a997e637f9105dc0ea98  (file)
  catalog 36c25c0f: not listed
  catalog 9da7c4a4 index 3
  @stream/image  type        raw image/jpeg
  @stream/image  attachment  camera.v1.FrameMeta  sha256:287bf0fa9f9251ed…
  state/info     type        camera.v1.Info       sha256:287bf0fa9f9251ed…

protobuf camera/v1/camera.proto  sha256:287bf0fa9f9251ed04a459d784019ede72c7aacb27cd9bf25ece4b98e54917fb
a raw type names a media type and no schema: its bytes are not a tool's to read (spec §7.2)
a revision a catalog does not list has no index there: a far side holding that catalog cannot read what is written under it (core §8.6)
the documents themselves: add --full, or name a resource

```
